  "engineering_boundaries": [
    "Illustrative Cambridge parcel and equipment routes; not a construction document.",
    "Drain-down tank capacities, expansion sizing, pipe slopes, complete drainability and restart controls remain to be engineered.",
    "Fresh-air dehumidification needs a suitably cold source and capacity sizing; the 75 F room-air loop alone does not establish a 50 F dew point.",
    "Rock properties and cooling savings require the specified test bore and thermal response testing.",
    "AI workload scenarios are modeled capacity estimates with transferred hardware-efficiency assumptions, not measured joules per token.",
    "Llama 3.1 405B is a heavy sizing proxy, not a verified best-quality model. The 2.5x Rubin rack throughput gain is transferred from R1 and requires validation.",
    "Full-workload figures are extrapolated capacity estimates. The existing six-campus geometry does not depict a designed 7.3–7.6 GW expansion.",
    "The $231–242B subtotal is compute-rack purchase only at an inherited $7.8M planning estimate per rack. A new total project cost and payback have not been established.",
    "Annual energy assumes full rated workload for 8,760 hours. Actual annual demand and utilization have not been forecast.",
    "Heavy-model context cache, storage bandwidth, additional support power and reliability reserves require validation. Old R1-specific memory figures do not establish heavy-model capacity."
  ],
